# 📘 Pronoun – Error Detection (50 Questions with Answers)

---

### **Q1.** Everyone should do **their** duty.

✅ Correct: Everyone should do **his/her** duty.

---

### **Q2.** Neither of the girls brought **their** book.

✅ Correct: Neither of the girls brought **her** book.

---

### **Q3.** One must take care of **themselves**.

✅ Correct: One must take care of **himself/herself**.

---

### **Q4.** Ram and Shyam are brothers. **He** is very intelligent.

✅ Correct: Ram and Shyam are brothers. **They** are very intelligent.

---

### **Q5.** This is the only one of my friends **who have** helped me.

✅ Correct: … **who has** helped me.

---

### **Q6.** It is **me** who is to blame.

✅ Correct: It is **I** who am to blame.

---

### **Q7.** Each of the boys in the class must do **their** homework.

✅ Correct: … must do **his** homework.

---

### **Q8.** Either of the two girls has lost **their** pen.

✅ Correct: … has lost **her** pen.

---

### **Q9.** Neither of the two brothers confessed **themselves** guilty.

✅ Correct: … confessed **himself** guilty.

---

### **Q10.** Anybody can do it if **they** try.

✅ Correct: … if **he/she** tries.

---

### **Q11.** One of my classmates has given **their** notes to me.

✅ Correct: … has given **his** notes.

---

### **Q12.** Neither Ravi nor his friends has completed **his** work.

✅ Correct: … has completed **their** work.

---

### **Q13.** Each of the players played well, didn’t **they**?

✅ Correct: … didn’t **he**?

---

### **Q14.** This is the man **whom** I think is honest.

✅ Correct: … the man **who** I think is honest.

---

### **Q15.** Between you and I, he is lazy.

✅ Correct: Between you and **me**, he is lazy.

---

### **Q16.** He as well as his friends have done **their** duty.

✅ Correct: … has done **his** duty.

---

### **Q17.** I, you and he must complete the work between **ourselves**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q18.** You and he should finish the job between **himself**.

✅ Correct: … between **yourselves**.

---

### **Q19.** Let you and I do the work.

✅ Correct: Let **you and me** do the work.

---

### **Q20.** You, he and I must finish **our** tasks in time.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q21.** Ramesh is one of those boys who has lost **his** book.

✅ Correct: … who have lost **their** books.

---

### **Q22.** The committee decided to postpone **their** meeting.

✅ Correct: … postponed **its** meeting.

---

### **Q23.** If anyone calls, tell **them** I am not at home.

✅ Correct: … tell **him/her** I am not at home.

---

### **Q24.** One should take care of **his** health.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q25.** You, he and I will complete this work by **myself**.

✅ Correct: … by **ourselves**.

---

### **Q26.** It is I who is to blame.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q27.** Either of the two girls have given **their** consent.

✅ Correct: Either … **has** given **her** consent.

---

### **Q28.** Neither of the two men were willing to sacrifice **their** life.

✅ Correct: … was willing to sacrifice **his** life.

---

### **Q29.** All except she were present.

✅ Correct: All except **her** were present.

---

### **Q30.** This is the boy **which** stood first in the class.

✅ Correct: … the boy **who** stood first.

---

### **Q31.** The two sisters quarrelled with **one another**.

✅ Correct: … quarrelled with **each other**.

---

### **Q32.** This is the only one of my friends who **have** passed.

✅ Correct: … who **has** passed.

---

### **Q33.** I and you must complete the work between **ourselves**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q34.** He is wiser than **me**.

✅ Correct: He is wiser than **I**.

---

### **Q35.** Nobody but him was praised.

✅ Correct: Nobody but **he** was praised.

---

### **Q36.** Everyone of the boys have done **their** work.

✅ Correct: … has done **his** work.

---

### **Q37.** Neither of the men are doing **their** duty.

✅ Correct: … is doing **his** duty.

---

### **Q38.** The two brothers love **each other**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q39.** You, he and I have completed **ours** work.

✅ Correct: … completed **our** work.

---

### **Q40.** The mother as well as her daughters have lost **their** ornaments.

✅ Correct: … has lost **her** ornaments.

---

### **Q41.** This is the same boy who has broken **his** toy.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q42.** You and he should complete the task between **yourselves**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q43.** I, you and he are guilty and should blame **ourselves**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q44.** All except **her** were present.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q45.** Between you and me, he is wrong.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q46.** Every boy and every girl has brought **their** book.

✅ Correct: … has brought **his** book.

---

### **Q47.** Neither Ravi nor his friends was ready to sacrifice **his** life.

✅ Correct: … were ready to sacrifice **their** lives.

---

### **Q48.** One must take care of **oneself**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q49.** The culprit confessed that he was guilty of having injured **himself**.

✅ Correct (no error).

---

### **Q50.** The students each gave **his** opinion.

✅ Correct (no error).

